# Stored flights: the flight list is part of the document (conditions + which configuration or motor), edited through the
# document (dirty dot, undo), saved in the `.bowshock` file and loaded back; results are not saved. The save/load round trip is
# unit-tested (`simulate::tests::flights_are_saved_with_the_file_and_loaded_back_without_results`).
#   cargo run -q -p bowshock -- drive --example crates/bowshock/scripts/flights.drive out/flights
viewport 1280x800

# Simulate: the example stores the kit's four flights; the document is clean.
click (625, 18)
screenshot FlightsStored-list.png

# Fly Nominal, then edit Windy's wind: the title gets its dirty dot and Nominal's result stays current (not faint).
click "Run"
click "Windy"
click (188, 448)
type "11"
type enter
screenshot FlightsStored-edit.png

# Add a flight: it starts from the selected one's conditions and is stored too.
click "compare +"
screenshot FlightsStored-added.png

# Undo the new flight (top bar): the list follows the document.
click (352, 20)
screenshot FlightsStored-undo.png

# Build and back: the flights are still there.
click (565, 18)
click (625, 18)
screenshot FlightsStored-back.png
